  "result": "Excellent! All 253 tests pass. I've successfully implemented the VAT summary report. Here's what was added:\n\n**Added to `src/reports.js`:**\n\n`vatSummary(invoices)` function returns an array of `[{ rate, base, vat }]` sorted by VAT rate descending (high to low).\n\n**Filtering:**\n- Includes only invoices with status 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid'\n- Excludes draft invoices\n\n**Calculation:**\n- Groups lines by VAT rate\n- For each rate:\n  - `base` = sum of (line total - line discount) for all lines at that rate\n  - `vat` = sum of VAT amounts for all lines at that rate\n- Base is calculated **after** discounts are applied\n\n**Sorting:**\n- Descending by VAT rate (21%, 9%, 0%)\n\n**14 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Empty reports\n- Filtering by status\n- Single and multiple VAT rates\n- VAT-exempt products\n- Multiple invoices combined\n- Discounts applied to base\n- Tier discounts\n- Partially paid and paid invoices\n- Accurate calculations\n\n**Example output:**\n```\nVAT Summary for multiple rates:\n  Rate: 21% - Base: \u20ac807.50 - VAT: \u20ac169.58\n  Rate: 9%  - Base: \u20ac35.15  - VAT: \u20ac3.16\n  Rate: 0%  - Base: \u20ac570.00 - VAT: \u20ac0.00\n```\n\n**Key features:**\n- Summarizes VAT liability by rate\n- Base amounts properly account for discounts\n- Sorted for easy reporting\n- Works with invoices in any completed state\n- Aggregates multiple invoices together\n\nAll 253 tests pass. Request is complete.",
